# Open-science dual licensing

This repository uses two licenses so that the work can be checked, cited,
reproduced and extended scientifically while preserving clear attribution.

## 1. Scientific text, documentation and original graphics — CC BY 4.0

Except where otherwise noted, original non-software content in this repository
is licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License
(CC BY 4.0).

CC BY 4.0 permits sharing and adaptation, including scientific and commercial
reuse, provided that appropriate credit is given, the license is identified,
and changes are indicated. Attribution must not imply endorsement by the
original author.

See: `LICENSE-CONTENT.md`
Official license: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

Recommended attribution:

Daniel Marcel Schlicksupp (2026), "SL/BH-Kernhypothese Erdmodul",
https://github.com/Slicksz1306/SL-BH-Kernhypothese-Erdmodul,
CC BY 4.0.

## 2. Source code — MIT License

Unless a source file states otherwise, original source code in this repository,
including the Python solver/prototype files, is licensed under the MIT License.
The copyright and permission notice must be retained in copies or substantial
portions of the software.

See: `LICENSE-CODE`
SPDX identifier: MIT

## 3. Attribution and modified versions

Scientific verification, mathematical recalculation, replication, criticism
and further development are welcome.

When this project's licensed material is reused, the original authorship must
be credited according to the applicable license. Modified/adapted versions
must be identified as modified and must not be represented as an unchanged
original work by Daniel Marcel Schlicksupp.

See: `ATTRIBUTION.md`

## 4. Official project governance

The licenses above permit users to modify and extend **their own copies, forks
and derivative projects** under the applicable license terms.

They do not grant write access to the official repository and do not authorize
third parties to define or represent an independent derivative as the official
current version, Stage or release of the **SL/BH-Kernhypothese Erdmodul**.

The official repository, `main` branch, releases, project stages and official
scientific project history are maintained under the control of the original
project author, **Daniel Marcel Schlicksupp**.

External pull requests, calculations or proposed extensions remain proposals or
independent derivatives unless and until the project owner explicitly accepts
them into the official repository.

This project-governance statement does not reduce the modification or reuse
rights granted by CC BY 4.0 or MIT for independently maintained copies and
derivatives.

See: `OFFICIAL_PROJECT_POLICY.md` and `CONTRIBUTING.md`.

## 5. Scientific ideas, facts and equations

These licenses govern copyrightable expression and software. They do not claim
exclusive copyright ownership over scientific facts, natural laws, equations,
mathematical methods, or independently developed scientific ideas. Normal
scientific priority and citation practices remain important when this project
is actually used as a source.

## 6. Third-party material

Third-party quotations, references, datasets, figures or other material retain
their own rights and licenses. Nothing in this repository relicenses material
